      "question": "Verify the distributive law $a \\times (b + c) = (a \\times b) + (a \\times c)$ for $a = -12$, $b = -8$, and $c = 15$.",
      "answer": "• **LHS Calculation**:\n  $$b + c = (-8) + 15 = 7$$\n  $$a \\times (b + c) = (-12) \\times 7 = -84$$\n• **RHS Calculation**:\n  $$a \\times b = (-12) \\times (-8) = +96$$\n  $$a \\times c = (-12) \\times 15 = -180$$\n  $$(a \\times b) + (a \\times c) = 96 + (-180) = -84$$\n• **Conclusion**:\n  $$\\text{LHS} = \\text{RHS} = -84$$\n  Hence, the distributive law of multiplication over addition is verified.",
